<!--
  EXAMPLE-ONLY scaffolding. Not part of the umbraco-multilingual skill and not shipped to users: a real
  site already has its own Document Types, and step 2 of the skill is making THOSE vary by culture.

  A culture-variant page type ('multilingualPage') with one variant property ('title') and one shared
  one ('code'), and a template that exercises every rendering piece the skill describes: the hreflang
  partial in <head>, the switcher partial, a variant value with Fallback.ToLanguage, and a dictionary
  item. Marker ids on the elements give the fixture something unambiguous to assert on.

  Block level variance: an INVARIANT 'blocks' Block List property whose element type
  ('multilingualBlock') varies by culture — the configuration the skill recommends. The template renders
  it twice: plainly, and with Fallback.ToLanguage, because an unexposed block behaves differently in
  each (omitted vs. shown in the fallback language, Umbraco 17.4+).

  Non-generic UmbracoViewPage because site 2 has no generated models.
-->
